// A marker typed through an input method, such as a full-width `＝`, is read as the marker, so the rest of the line is still checked.

@actor mira
    name：Mira
//      ^ PIB1044
    pose： happy、sad
//      ^ PIB1044
//             ^ PIB1044
    pose ＋＝ angry
//       ^^ PIB1044
@channel mood： calm、tense
//           ^ PIB1044
//                 ^ PIB1044
// A display name is text, so it can hold any of them.
@actor rex
    name: ＡＩ「助手」：＝

== fixture.forms
@set ＄met ＝ true
//   ^ PIB1044
//        ^ PIB1044
@set ￥met = true
//   ^ PIB1044
@jump ime。case
//       ^ PIB1044
@pause ０。５s
//     ^^^ PIB1044
@if has_item（“key”）
//          ^^ PIB1044
//               ^^ PIB1044
    mira: Found it.
mira: Wait{if $met ＝＝ true}, yes{/if}.
//                 ^^ PIB1044
mira: [b」Bold[/b].
//      ^ PIB1044
-> Go @if $met ＠once
//             ^ PIB1044
@set ＄met ＝
//   ^ PIB1044
//        ^ PIB1044
//         ^ PIB1046

// At a line's start, a header, an `@` line or an option typed this way still makes that line, so the lines after it keep their place.

＝＝ fixture.lines
// PIB1044
＠if $met
// PIB1044
    mira: Yes.
ー＞ はい
// PIB1044
    mira: OK.
－> いいえ
// PIB1044
-》 好的
// PIB1044
@sequence
    - one
    ー　two
//  ^ PIB1044
    － three
//  ^ PIB1044

// Must not trigger

\＠if is text, and so is \＝＝.
ーっと待って。
＝ is one sign.
ー
mira: She said “hi” and left, ＝＝ then 「b」.
mira（happy）：Hi.
@set $quote = "he said “hi” to 「me」"
@jump ime.case // 「メモ」：＝
